fix(exec-sync): the CALLED rollup cannot extract payload server-side

The production backfill (card 3fd5bf3b-9510-81bf-9ea5-ca5e2f3a1282, §9
step 3) crashed on tick 10 after ~21.4k runs had landed:

    psycopg2.errors.UntranslatableCharacter:
    unsupported Unicode escape sequence
      at exec_sync._fetch_called -> SQL_CALLED

SQL_CALLED grouped on `e.payload->>'name'`. This module's docstring already
said the payload is never cast server-side because it holds literal \u0000 —
but it carved out `->>` over a single key as safe, and that carve-out is
wrong: `run_events.payload` is `json`, not `jsonb`, so a text-backed document
has to be parsed in full to reach any part of it, and the NUL fails the
conversion. Verified straight against the production table, outside this code
path:

    SELECT count(*) FROM run_events e
     WHERE e.kind='tool_call' AND e.payload->>'name' IS NOT NULL;
    DETAIL:  \u0000 cannot be converted to text.

There is therefore no narrower server-side form to retreat to. The rollup is
now derived from the tool-call rows SQL_TOOL_CALLS has already fetched and
psycopg has already parsed client-side, which is exact rather than
approximate -- both used the identical predicate with no LIMIT, so they always
described the same row set -- and it drops a whole query per batch.

Ticks 1-9 passed only because no payload in those watermark windows carried a
NUL, which is why the schema-shaped test that asserted the carve-out was green
throughout. That test now asserts the rule that actually holds, over every
SQL_* attribute, and the fake cursor REFUSES any server-side payload
extraction so a mock can no longer pass where production fails. Plus the crash
itself as a test, and the rollup's own counting/empty-name behaviour.

Mutation-checked: restoring the old server-side rollup fails 11 tests.

